# The negation of a BallVector with one-limb centers (milestone2.md, "BallVector": bv_neg_k): each
# center negated (neg_1), the radius unchanged (bv_neg_radius): exact, the result is exactly the set
# of the negated members. The state is that of norm_upper_1 on the centers written, as for every ball
# vector, and the finish norm_finish_1: the operand that is the whole space (radius +infinity) gives
# the whole space, every center written zero.
fold:          bv_neg_1
arrays:        stored x
scalars:       stored rx
state:         m, mask ok
step:          z = neg_1(x)
record:        (m, ok) = norm_step_1(m, ok, z)
combine:       (m, ok) = norm_combine(m, ok, m, ok)
radius:        rz = bv_neg_radius(m, rx)
finish:        (r, finite) = norm_finish_1(rz, ok)
orders:        sequential, lanes
writes:        z
output:        r
output:        mask finite
value:         -x
requires:      ball_vector x rx
ensures:       encloses_entries z r -x x=x,rx flag=finite finite_when=abs_le(abs(x)+rx,1) radii_when=abs_le(rx,1) exact
min_precision: 1
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
source:        the negation of each center, the radius of ball_neg_1 (milestone2.md, BallVector)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
